      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Panther Burn has inspired music and literature, from Jimmy Phillips’ songs to Curlew’s experimental jazz and the 2009 novel The Children of Panther Burn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/panther_burn_mississippi",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Situated on the flat, alluvial plains of the Mississippi Delta, Panther Burn sits on deep, fertile soils deposited by the river’s ancient sediments.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/panther_burn_mississippi",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Big Sunflower River and Deer Creek run through the area, draining into the Yazoo Basin and exposing Panther Burn to periodic floodplain inundation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
